{
 "id": "2026-11-20-shenzhen-declaration",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Three nuclear powers at one table in China. So what did they actually agree?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "For the first time, the leaders of the US, China and Russia met as a trio, in Shenzhen at the APEC summit. They issued a Declaration toward Peace. All three say a nuclear war cannot be won and must never be fought."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "But the text only promises a dialogue on nuclear risks. No arms cuts, no timetable. It also backs more refined fuel supply and vague UN reform, and warns the International Criminal Court not to abuse its powers. That court issued a warrant for Putin in 2023."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Ukraine, reports say, is not mentioned at all. Afterwards, Putin told reporters that after the strikes on the Crimean Bridge, Russia will not negotiate a ceasefire. He promised a response far more painful than Kyiv's attack."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Shenzhen lead to real nuclear talks next year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
